# M6 — Honest Product Workspaces And Application Catalog

Make the product topology reflect canonical objects without moving truth or authority into the shell.

## Why this is next

`sequence.v1.json` places M6 at canonical build step 6 with `depends_on: ["M5"]`, and M5 chains
M4 → M3. Those stages produce the generic pursuit/result seam, the OutcomeRoom System spine, and the
participant/frontier reads a product surface can honestly project. M6 adds the normalized
surface-definition split, the daemon-admitted catalog compiler, and typed Systems/Work views over
those reads; static shadow compilation may run earlier, permanent migration may not.

