## In scope

- `M6.1` complete the normalized product-surface definition/release/installation/System-interface/serving record split.
- `M6.2` make the catalog compiler daemon-admitted, request-scoped, policy-filtered, tenant-safe, and context-safe.
- `M6.3` make Systems render identity, constitution, lifecycle, package, desired/observed topology, work, authority, evidence, improvement, and interfaces without owning them.
- `M6.4` make Work render typed GoalRun, OutcomeRoom, AutomationRun, Session, WorkItem, WorkRun, queue, review, incident, and history subjects.
- `M6.5` stop new generic Mission writes and resolve legacy records to one typed backing subject through reviewable alias/migration receipts.
- `M6.6` keep Governance as decision surface, Operations as admitted infrastructure/member action surface, and Provenance as evidence projection.
- `M6.7` make Packages own local package lifecycle while Marketplace remains optional discovery/commerce.
- `M6.8` preserve direct Session, Project, Automation, and stand-alone GoalRun creation without forced System genesis.
- `M6.9` close the post-taxonomy `UX-00` seed-coverage ledger against the current application topology.
- `M6.10` migrate canonical routes/navigation only after typed aliases preserve query, hash, embed, return path, Project, System, and subject context.
- `M6.11` treat generated React or other domain applications as replaceable System-interface packages and projections; neither one UI instance nor multiple UI replicas becomes the System, its runtime truth, or its failover/coordination layer.
- `M6.12` deliver Settings as the sixth core workspace at `/settings`, project every pane from its canonical owner, persist preferences through daemon/Agentgres optimistic revision checks, and keep transient UI state local.
- `M6.13` delete legacy route handlers and return the typed `410` retirement refusal; contextual route resolution must never become compatibility aliasing.
- Own `sdk-cli-adk-odk-builder-journey` for supported interface and maturity-labeled builder parity; the docs module supplies runnable documentation but does not become a second sequence.
- Require the existing M6 aggregate to join the builder record; runnable interface evidence does not grant client-side authority.
- Own the operational-journey records for Home, Systems, Projects, Applications, Work, Automations, Packages, and Developer Workspace, whose selected backend prerequisites are M1–M5, and join those eight records in the aggregate; pull all five core workspaces, twelve owner applications, two substrate applications, conditional Embodied Systems registration, and extension/tool projections.

## Out of scope

- Operational depth for any registered surface beyond this stage's own journeys; that belongs to the later-stage owner record and aggregate named in the approved work-item map.
- Local ontology and action semantics (M7); the terminal internal/external product journeys that close the P1–P3 claim levels (M9); the Operations operational journey (M10); and live Embodied Systems depth (M11) — M6 carries conditional Embodied Systems *registration* only.
- Backend read models themselves — M1–M5 own them, M6 projects them; and making Marketplace mandatory or letting commerce gate local package lifecycle.
- Treating route, registry, screenshot, seed, or pixel parity as product membership or as depth.
- Creating or editing a record here does not implement behavior, activate work, close a literal exit, or change a stage.

