## Exit proof

Bound to the aggregate work item `m6-product-surface-and-typed-workspaces` (`sequence.v1.json`
`exit_gate.kind: aggregate_exit`). The stage may be declared complete only when all of the following
hold and retained evidence contains exactly one literal `M6_PRODUCT_SURFACE_AND_TYPED_WORKSPACES_EXIT=0`:

- shell, catalog, command palette, contextual launch, and API projections compile from one registered source;
- no draft, recalled, disabled, unavailable, foreign-tenant, or unbound surface becomes launchable;
- every tool has one owner breadcrumb;
- no surface is promoted by screenshot, capture, pixel parity, or copied taxonomy;
- Systems and Work expose honest empty, denied, unavailable, degraded, recovery, and completed states;
- product-usability thresholds in the selected cohort are frozen and met;
- separate bounded records close for the normalized compiler; source/serve convergence; production fixture-fallback retirement; shell/alias migration and accessibility; Systems and Work; consequential-action authority/receipt convergence; current-source surface disposition; and honest registration/routing/loading/empty/denied/unavailable/degraded states for every pulled core/owner/substrate surface;
- a closed projection maps each admitted surface to the exact later-stage operational-journey owner listed in the approved work-item map.

## Blocks advancement

- The M5 aggregate `m5-selected-profile-exit-proof` and the verifier `m5-p0-readiness-verifier` are unmet, or the cross-stage dependencies `m0-canon-owner-coverage-and-orphan-verifier` (M0), `project-discovery-startup-and-session-chain` (M2), and `m3-direct-path-and-exit-proof` (M3) are unmet.
- Any of the seventeen children is not `verified`; every child disposition is `unconditional_active`, so none may be waived.
- `PG-1.2` (builder journey) or `PG-2.2` (consequential-action authority) is unmapped or unmet, or any canon gap below remains unresolved by its named owner, since R-CONTRACT cannot bind an unregistered contract family.
- Frozen metric thresholds are breached: nonzero unauthorized/wrong-final-invoker calls, nonzero duplicate or status-inferred effects, nonzero unresolved owner/dependency mappings, or any consequential product control lacking owner, final-invoker, authority, receipt, and negative-path disposition.

## Nonclaims

- Operational depth for every registered surface. Route presence, registration, reference capture, pixel parity, or an M6 shell-state exit cannot establish operational depth; it is proved only by the applicable later-stage owner record and aggregate.
- Screenshot or registry parity does not establish product membership; no operational-depth claim is made for unbuilt owners, and no stage closes by declaration.
- Neither one UI instance nor multiple UI replicas becomes the System, its runtime truth, or its failover/coordination layer.
- Runnable builder/interface evidence does not grant client-side authority, and runnable documentation does not become a second sequence.

